{"id": "EUVD-2026-86635", "enisaUuid": "4b98e5b5-3c13-3044-93b6-c28244ed0edc", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: ethernet: cortina: Count dropped frames as NAPI work\n\nThe RX loop only consumes budget when it successfully delivers a frame.\nError paths keep consuming descriptors without reducing the budget, so a\nstream of bad frames can process the entire receive ring in one poll.\n\nMove the budget accounting to a common end-of-frame path. This counts\neach completed frame as NAPI work whether it was delivered or dropped,\nmatching the behavior of the vendor driver.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:23:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:11:48", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/620b7184808b25cf58268856f892b9ba83c181fd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9620e2ce9b5998ebbf157241f296f8ddb92285c2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/27b5753077d1cfda5fe201d2ba602de76a9a09b1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e858b9b1ea3cbbc353189d07dec40dc16967e290", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/58140f1cebb776d174dc6ff41c15401654a5b1ea", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cceb6cd7f0e5ed2944a9ca22443d7b9da82f60ab", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5754e0c0758805096ecfeaf4c1b146ad51ed246f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b856c552f556bc0341c1dbe0bf88e630fd1dc4b7"], "aliases": ["GHSA-qrx6-pjc4-f5p5", "CVE-2026-97981"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1569813f-f825-368f-ac78-53926a8e0301", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "1956796b-4bb5-3251-8c7c-2ac2d681e4d6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "25a54279-f9e1-3066-9145-88ca5bc16dfa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "415a15ad-a942-3b33-8488-64b5c936c0d0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "pro